msgid "``em.catalogs`` — the datamodel's catalogues, read only (MICRO-SEG09, 21 Nov 2026)."
msgstr ""

msgid "E.D.: «ci sono tutti i data object di s3dgraphy?». The node and edge TYPES were already there (``em.graph`` returns them, ``reference/types`` has a page for each); the catalogues of ``JSON_config`` were read only inside the library. Here they are, as the library reads them — the EM language's own tables, not the logic of any one tool::"
msgstr ""

msgid "Every function answers a COPY (as :class:`~s3dgraphy.em.GraphView` does): what a script changes in it changes nothing in the datamodel. The qualia, extractor and document types here are the CORE ones; with the active packages added they are :data:`em.profiles <s3dgraphy.em.profiles>` (``qualia_types()``, ``extractor_types()``, ``document_types()``). The epochs and groups of a document are nodes of its graph (``em.graph.nodes(type=\"EpochNode\")``, ``em.graph.chronology()``); the vocabularies are :data:`em.vocab <s3dgraphy.em.vocab>`; the DTC is its node types and :func:`em.stamp <s3dgraphy.em.stamp>`."
msgstr ""

